Lowell,[ after all], is[ where] she found inspiration to pick up a paintbrush again[ at age] 40. Her success as a full-time working artist in Paris is proof, she says, that it’s never[ too] late to pursue a dream.
Slogging along the daily grind,[ McCl]uskey’s art supplies ended up in boxes in a basement. She carried[ old] photos of her favorite works with her as a reminder from[ time to] time of who she was before becoming a mom, a wife and a cubicle dweller[.]
