After breakfast climb the 5th century Sigiriya rock fortress which is a world heritage site,[ built] by King Kashy[apa (]477[-]495 AD). The 'Lion Rock' is a citadel of unusual beauty[ rising] 200 meters from the scrub jungle[.] The rock was the innermost stronghold of the 70 hectare fortified town. Visit the world[-]renowned frescoes of the 'Heavenly Maidens' of Sigiriya, which are in a sheltered pocket of the rock approached by a spiral stairway[.] These frescoes are painted in earth pigments on plaster[.]
